WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.747
Constraints turn important business rules into rules

00:00:02.774 --> 00:00:06.855
the database can enforce NOT NULL says

00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:10.147
a value is required DEFAULT supplies a

00:00:10.173 --> 00:00:13.489
value when one is omitted UNIQUE protects

00:00:13.516 --> 00:00:17.345
candidate keys or other non-duplicate rules CHECK

00:00:17.358 --> 00:00:21.476
evaluates a Boolean condition PRIMARY KEY defines

00:00:21.489 --> 00:00:25.516
row identity FOREIGN KEY protects relationships to

00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:30.061
parent rows One beginner detail is especially

00:00:30.088 --> 00:00:32.640
important CHECK does not automatically make a

00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:36.833
column required For example a check that

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.478
quantity is greater than zero only evaluates

00:00:39.491 --> 00:00:41.386
the quantity when a value is present

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.007
If quantity must always be present combine

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.780
the check with NOT NULL The database

00:00:48.807 --> 00:00:51.570
should enforce important rules whenever possible
instead

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:53.675
of relying only on application code or

00:00:53.702 --> 00:00:54.557
user memory
